  "description": "NASGAR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H86 Mn2 N12 O22 Sm4,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Sm1F (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2F (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1F (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.334-3.873 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.14-129.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H86Mn2N12O22Sm4·2(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Sm(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
